# CartRadar global config.
# Copy this file to .env.local (git-ignored) and fill in the values. Expo reads it for local runs;
# on Vercel the same EXPO_PUBLIC_* names are set as project environment variables.
#
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_*  are copied into the app bundle. Anyone who opens the app can read them. URLs and public ids only, never secrets.
#   everything else is for local scripts only. The deployed secrets (BEE_TOKEN, OPENAI_API_KEY, ALLOWED_EMAILS)
#   live in Supabase, see supabase/functions/.env.example.

# ---------- Supabase (login, cloud storage and the Edge Functions) ----------
# Create a project at https://supabase.com, then run supabase/migrations/0001_init.sql in its SQL editor.
# Project URL and anon key are under Project Settings, API. Both are public by design: row level security
# decides what each user can read, so they are safe in the bundle. NEVER put the service_role key in the app.
# Leave both empty to turn login off; the app then keeps everything on the device (and Bee sync is unavailable).
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Google sign-in (browser only for now):
# 1. Create an OAuth client of type "Web application" at https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
#    and add http://localhost:8081 and your Vercel URL (https://<project>.vercel.app) under "Authorized JavaScript origins".
# 2. In Supabase, Authentication, Providers, Google: enable it and enter that client id and secret.
# 3. In Supabase, Authentication, URL Configuration: set Site URL to your Vercel URL.
# The client id is public, not a secret. The login screen only shows the Google button when this is set.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=

# ---------- Local accuracy checks only (npm run check-demo, npm run check-sample) ----------
# The app never reads these. The deployed extract-items function uses the OPENAI_* secrets in Supabase instead.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
